# Poisons for Alliance Rogues: Mathias and the Defias (2360) and Klaven's
# Tower (2359) from Master Mathias Shaw to Agent Kearnen on the Westfall side
# of the Duskwood border and back, then the follow-up The Touch of Zanzil
# (2607, 2608, 2609) with Doc Mixilpixil in the SI:7 cellar.
# Forever change (Forever's Rogue class quest list,
# data/local/quest-audit/): Klaven's Tower now
# teaches Poisons (Forever moved it from the trainer onto this quest).
# Rewards from the same list:
# Recipe: Thistle Tea (Klaven's Tower), Eau de Mixilpixil (The Touch of
# Zanzil, 2609). Forever's quest data files Klaven's Tower as a group quest.
# Sources: quests.json, npcs.json, objects.json and items.json for the givers,
# drops, vendors and places. The KB drops table: the Defias Tower Key 100%
# from the Malformed Defias Drone (level 23, one spawn). Forever's server data
# (gameobject_template): the Duskwood Chest has the same lock as Gallywix's
# Lockbox on the Horde side (about 70-75 Lockpicking by players' notes).
# data/local/mechanics (quest-steps and quest-notes, checked 2026-10-20):
# Kearnen's tree, the sparkling drone and its loop, the chest's poison that
# lets the drone see you, the chest's 1 second respawn, the /lay emote, the
# reagents' shops, the spool's two spawns and the Bronze Tube's small stock.
# Klaven Mortwake (level 26 elite) on the top floor, Sap: npcs.json and
# players' notes; the jump onto the bookshelf by the chest: a Forever
# leveling guide (2026).
# alliance/04-redridge-mountains and alliance/05-duskwood do 2360 and 2359 on
# the route; this guide repeats them for anyone off it and adds The Touch of
# Zanzil.

step Mathias and the Defias
  zone Stormwind City
  tip At 20 Master Mathias Shaw, upstairs in the SI:7 building in Old Town, sends you to Agent Kearnen in Westfall. This chain is how you learn Poisons on Forever, so do not skip it.
  level 20
  accept 2360                                 -- Master Mathias Shaw

step Agent Kearnen
  zone Westfall
  tip Kearnen hides stealthed against the west side of a big tree with two small trees in front of it, just north of Klaven Mortwake's Defias tower in the far east of Westfall, by the Duskwood border. Read Kearnen's Journal for the tower's layout if you like.
  turnin 2360                                 -- Agent Kearnen
  accept 2359

step The Defias Tower Key
  tip Get the key first. The Malformed Defias Drone (level 23, not elite) starts at the tower entrance and walks a loop around the outside; it is the spiky-haired one trailing yellow sparkles. Stealth up and Pick Pocket it from behind: it always has the key. It hits hard: if stealth breaks, Sprint away. Watch for the pair of Defias Drones that also patrol.
  collect 7923 quest 2359.2 "Pick Pocket the Malformed Defias Drone for the Defias Tower Key"

step Klaven's journal
  tip Sneak up the tower. Defias Tower Patrollers (23) and Sentries (24) guard the floors; an Ambush with a dagger kills them outright if you would rather clear them. Klaven Mortwake, a level 26 elite, waits on the top floor: Sap him, or bring a friend. The Duskwood Chest beside his desk needs Lockpicking of about 70-75 (practise on the boxes at Alther's Mill in Redridge first). A trick: while the Sentries are away, jump from the chair to the lamp to the bookshelf above the chest, step out of stealth and open the chest from there. Opening it poisons you with the Touch of Zanzil, which stops your stealth for a while and lets the drone see you; that is why the key comes first. Then get out.
  collect 7908 quest 2359.1 @70.4,74.0        -- Klaven Mortwake's Journal: the Duskwood Chest, top floor

step Master Mathias Shaw
  zone Stormwind City
  tip Head north through Elwynn to Stormwind; Mathias Shaw is upstairs in SI:7. He teaches Poisons and gives you the Thistle Tea recipe. Poisons are made, not bought: each batch of Instant Poison takes a Dust of Decay and an Empty Vial, which Jasper Fel and Sloan McCoy sell in Old Town next to SI:7. Buy a stack of each, open Poisons from your spellbook to make them, then use a poison on your weapon.
  turnin 2359 reward 18160                    -- Master Mathias Shaw: Poisons
  accept 2607

step Doc Mixilpixil
  tip The Touch of Zanzil still sits on you. Doc Mixilpixil works in the cellar of the SI:7 building: the stairs down are under the stairs to the upper floor, behind Jasper Fel. Target him and type /lay (nothing after it) to be examined, then wait. If he does nothing, abandon the quest, take it again and wait until he asks you to lie down.
  turnin 2607                                 -- Doc Mixilpixil
  accept 2608
  complete 2608 @80.06,69.9 live              -- /lay with the Doc targeted
  turnin 2608
  accept 2609

step The cure's ingredients
  tip All four are in Stormwind. Simple Wildflowers: Bernard or Felicia Gump's flower shop by the Trade District canal. A Leaded Vial: many general goods and alchemy vendors (Keldric Boucher, Jasper Fel and others). A Bronze Tube: the Auction House in the Trade District; the engineering suppliers keep only one and are nearly always sold out, and an engineer can make one. The Spool of Light Chartreuse Silk Thread lies on the floor beside the left end of the counter in The Finest Thread, the tailor's shop on the canals; you can only pick it up with this quest. If you skip the cure, an Anti-Venom (First Aid) or a druid's Cure Poison also clears the Touch of Zanzil.
  buy 3421 x1 nearest                         -- Simple Wildflowers
  buy 3372 x1 nearest                         -- Leaded Vial
  collect 4371 x1 @61.2,71.3 map 1453 live    -- Bronze Tube: the Auction House
  collect 8431 quest 2609.4                   -- Spool of Light Chartreuse Silk Thread

step Back to Doc Mixilpixil
  turnin 2609 reward 8432                     -- Doc Mixilpixil: Eau de Mixilpixil
